.TH YANASNET 1 "2026-11-23" "yanas net 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yanas net \- deterministic Layer-2/Layer-3 network simulator
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B netsim
[\fIoptions\fR] [\fIfile\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yanas net
simulates IPv4/Ethernet networks (ARP, VLAN/802.1Q, MAC-learning switches,
spanning tree, static routing, ICMP) on a deterministic logical clock.
It runs an interactive command prompt, line-command scripts, Lua scripts, or
loads \fB.yn\fR scene files. The prompt supports history, Tab completion, and
Emacs-style line editing. It is an offline simulator: protocol stacks are
simulated and do not connect to, bridge, or replace a live network stack.
Press Ctrl-C to interrupt a running simulation.
Diagnostics include \fBdevices\fR, \fBlinks\fR, \fBports\fR, \fBroutes\fR,
\fBroutes6\fR, \fBarp-table\fR, \fBnd6-table\fR, \fBmac-table\fR, \fBstats\fR, \fBdrop-stats\fR (drop reasons), \fBtraceroute\fR, and \fBexport dot|svg\fR.
IPv6 host addressing, Neighbor Discovery, ICMPv6 echo/errors, \fBtraceroute6\fR
and ping timeouts (\fBset-ip6\fR/\fBping6\fR/\fBtraceroute6\fR), connected/static routes (\fBadd-route6\fR), IPv6 gateways
(\fBset-gateway6\fR), router forwarding with NDP next-hop resolution, and
\fBnd6-table\fR diagnostics.
UDP echo (\fBudp-echo\fR/\fBudp-send\fR), a real TCP service and client
(\fBtcp-listen\fR/\fBtcp-connect\fR/\fBtcp-send\fR) with MSS/window-scale negotiation, SACK,
RTT-based retransmission, RST, keepalive, zero-window persist, simultaneous
open/close, timestamps, delayed ACK/Nagle, SACK/DSACK recovery, SYN backlog and
cookies, Reno/CUBIC-style congestion control, TLP/PRR/RACK recovery, optional
pacing, collision-checked ephemeral ports, ECN marking, MTU-aware TCP MSS,
path-MTU discovery with DF and ICMP Fragmentation Needed, data re-segmentation,
basic upward PMTU re-probing, IPv4 fragmentation/reassembly, and \fBtcp-status\fR diagnostics; the deprecated
\fBtcp-lite-*\fR legacy lightweight transport (not TCP); a DHCP server/client
(\fBdhcp-server\fR/\fBdhcp-client\fR/\fBdhcp-relay\fR) with lease renewal,
rebind, expiry/reclaim, \fBdhcp-lease-time\fR and \fBdhcp-release\fR; a DNS
server and resolver
(\fBdns-server\fR/\fBdns-record\fR/\fBdns-cname\fR/\fBdns-query\fR) with
configurable TTL and client caching; PTR and MX records; negative caching with
SOA TTL; resolver failover/retry, EDNS0 and DNS-over-TCP fallback, authoritative
zones, NS delegation (glue and no-glue), wildcard records, AXFR zone transfer
with source ACLs and TSIG authentication, dynamic UPDATE/prerequisites,
AAAA records, per-RRset TTLs, primary/secondary NOTIFY/AXFR replication with SOA
refresh/expire timers, IXFR journal/diagnostics/refresh fallback, bounded LRU
caching and TTL clamps; source NAT/PAT and port
forwarding (\fBnat\fR/\fBnat-port\fR/\fBnat-table\fR); RIP v2-lite dynamic
routing (\fBrip\fR/\fBrip-status\fR); and an OSPFv2 implementation with
per-area LSDB/SPF and ABR Type 3/4 summaries, Type 5 external routes/default
origination/redistribution, area summaries, stub/NSSA areas (Type 7 translation), interface
cost/passive policy and
simple-password, MD5, SHA-1 or SHA-256
authentication (\fBospf\fR/\fBospf-status\fR/\fBospf-auth\fR/\fBospf-cost\fR/\fBospf-passive\fR/\fBospf-area\fR). Router
\fBacl\fR/\fBacl6\fR rules, \fBset-link ... loss|dup|jitter|mtu|clear\fR impairment,
\fBspan\fR ingress port mirroring, an ASCII
\fBmap\fR, \fBhelp <command>\fR, and \fBgenerate tree\fR are also available.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Show usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-features
List build features (e.g. \fBlua\fR) and exit.
.TP
.B \-q, \-\-quiet
Suppress status lines such as \fBran; now=\fR and \fBdone; now=\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keep-going
Continue after a script error instead of stopping at the first one.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-lua
Refuse to execute \fB.lua\fR scripts (defense in depth beyond the default sandbox).
.TP
.B \-i, \-\-interactive
Enter the interactive prompt after loading a file.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Emit NDJSON records (requires a file).
.TP
.B \-\-log \fIfile\fR
Also append JSON records to a file.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-file \fIpath\fR
Run a scene or script file.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I *.yn
Scene file (JSON) with devices, ports, IPv4/IPv6 addresses, links, STP/routing/gateway/ACL/NAT/SPAN settings, and an
optional layout array (ignored by the CLI).
.TP
.I *.txt
Line-command script.
.TP
.I *.lua
Lua scenario script (sandboxed by default; see SECURITY).
.SH LIMITS
Devices 4096; ports 65536 (1024 per device); links 65536; event queue 5,000,000;
pcap 2,000,000 frames / 256 MiB; scripts 16 MiB / 1,000,000 lines; scenes
100,000 commands; Lua 4 MiB / 50M instructions.
.SH SECURITY
Lua scripts run in a restricted sandbox: only the base library (without
\fBdofile\fR, \fBload\fR, \fBloadfile\fR, \fBrequire\fR) plus \fBstring\fR,
\fBtable\fR, \fBmath\fR, \fButf8\fR, and \fBcoroutine\fR are available;
\fBos\fR, \fBio\fR, \fBpackage\fR, and \fBdebug\fR are not loaded. A per-run
instruction budget and a script-size limit stop runaway scripts. Use
\fB\-\-no\-lua\fR to disable Lua entirely.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 on runtime/script errors, 2 on usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
netsim
netsim tests/config.yn
netsim -i tests/config.yn
netsim tests/auto_ping.txt
netsim tests/lua_ping.lua
netsim examples/13_ospf.txt
.fi
